-- title:
--   Index and cusp count of Γ₁(Mp) versus Γ₁(M)
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and let $p$ be a prime not dividing $M$. Two equalities of natural numbers are asserted, both inside $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$. First, the index of the subgroup generated by $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ together with the integer powers of $-1$, namely $\Gamma_1(Mp) \sqcup \langle -1\rangle$, equals $(p^2-1)$ times the index of $\Gamma_1(M) \sqcup \langle -1\rangle$; here $p^2-1$ is truncated natural subtraction, harmless since $p \ge 2$. Second, the number of double cosets of the underlying set of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ against the underlying set of the subgroup generated by the powers of $T = \begin{pmatrix}1&1\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ together with the powers of $-1$, i.e. the cardinality of $\Gamma_1(Mp)\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\langle T,-1\rangle$ as a `Nat.card`, equals $2(p-1)$ times the corresponding number $\#\,\Gamma_1(M)\backslash \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/\langle T,-1\rangle$.
--
--   These are the classical multiplicativity statements for the index of $\Gamma_1(N)\{\pm 1\}$ and for the number of cusps of $\Gamma_1(N)$ when the level is multiplied by a prime not dividing it, the bound $M \ge 5$ being needed for the cusp count. Both numbers feed the genus comparison for the modular curves $X_1(Mp)$ and $X_1(M)$, which is where this result is used.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CongruenceSubgroup_index_gamma1_mul_and_natCard_doubleCoset_gamma1_mul_of_prime_of_not_dvd.lean

